<title>USA: NYC $45 mln repriced, top yield cut to 5.75 pct.</title>
<headline>NYC $45 mln repriced, top yield cut to 5.75 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morgan Stanley &amp; Co said Thursday it repriced New York City's $44.9 million bond deal, lowering yields in the 2016 and 2026 maturities to 5.68 percent and 5.75 percent, respectively.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:</p>
<p>NEW YORK CITY</p>
<p>RE: $44,890,000*</p>
<p>EDUCATIONAL CONSTRUCTION FUND</p>
<p>JUNIOR SUBORDINATED REVENUE BONDS, SERIES 1996</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD RECEIVED</p>
<p>PLEASE NOTE COUPON CHANGE IN 2010 AND YIELD</p>
<p>CHANGES IN 2016 AND 2026.</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: Aaa		   S&amp;P: AAA</p>
<p>AMBAC INSURED</p>
<p>    DATED: 09/15/1996	  FIRST COUPON: 04/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 04/01</p>
<p>MATURITY		 AMOUNT*    COUPON	   PRICE</p>
<p>04/01/1999		  740M    4.25  %	  4.35</p>
<p>04/01/2000		  770M    4.50  %	  4.55</p>
<p>04/01/2001		  805M    4.60  %	  4.70</p>
<p>04/01/2002		  845M    4.70  %	  4.80</p>
<p>04/01/2003		  885M    4.80  %	  4.90</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>04/01/2004		  925M    5.00  %	100.00</p>
